2026-09-17T15:01:03.4753601Z       "body": "## Pull Request\r\n\r\nDiscussion: #16362 \r\n\r\n## Description\r\n\r\nThis PR improves typing for `OpenAPI tag metadata` by introducing `TypedDict` definitions for the OpenAPI tag structure.\r\n\r\nThe goal is to provide better IDE autocomplete and static type checking for fields such as name, description, and `externalDocs`, while preserving backward compatibility with existing code using `list[dict[str, Any]]`.\r\n\r\nThe parameter accepts both forms:\r\n\r\n`list[OpenAPITag] | list[dict[str, Any]] | None`\r\n## AI Disclaimer\r\n\r\n<!-- If using AI, write here the prompt and model used -->\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary>AI transcript</summary>\r\n\r\n<!-- Paste here the entire AI transcript -->\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n## Checklist\r\n\r\n- [x] This PR links to a GitHub Discussion for the proposed code change.\r\n- [ ] I added tests for the change.\r\n- [ ] The new or updated tests fail on the main branch and pass on this PR.\r\n- [ ] Coverage stays at 100%.\r\n- [ ] The documentation explains the change if needed.\r\n",
